    "cause": "The Bash app_alias builds the alias string incorrectly: it places TF_ALIAS before the alias command and omits TF_CMD, causing the generated alias to miss the expected \"TF_CMD=$(TF_ALIAS\" part required by the tests.",
    "fix": "    def app_alias(self, fuck):\n        # Build the alias so that TF_CMD expands a command that includes TF_ALIAS and other env vars.\n        # The alias should look like:\n        # alias fuck='TF_CMD=$(TF_ALIAS=fuck PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 TF_SHELL_ALIASES=$(alias) thefuck $(fc -ln -1)) && eval $TF_CMD'\n        alias = (\n            \"alias {0}='TF_CMD=$(TF_ALIAS={0} PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8 \"\n            \"TF_SHELL_ALIASES=$(alias) thefuck $(fc -ln -1)) && eval $TF_CMD\".format(fuck)\n        )\n        if settings.alter_history:\n            return alias + \" && history -s $TF_CMD'\"\n        else:\n            return alias + \"'\"\n  ",
    "confidence": "high",
    "valid": true,
    "locations": [
      {
        "file": "thefuck/shells/zsh.py",
        "function": "Zsh.app_alias",
        "fix": "    def app_alias(self, alias_name):\n        # Build the alias so that TF_ALIAS is set inside the TF_CMD substitution,\n        # mirroring the Bash implementation and satisfying the expected pattern.\n        alias = (\n            \"alias {0}='TF_CMD=$(TF_ALIAS={0}\"\n            \" PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8\"\n            \" TF_SHELL_ALIASES=$(alias)\"\n            \" thefuck $(fc -ln -1 | tail -n 1)) && eval $TF_CMD\".format(alias_name)\n        )\n\n        if settings.alter_history:\n            return alias + \" && print -s $TF_CMD'\"\n        else:\n            return alias + \"'\"\n"
      }
    ],
